---
import LegalPage from '~/layouts/LegalPage.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL as CONTACT } from '~/lib/contact';
import { LICENCE_URLS } from '~/lib/gbif/licence';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms and credits"
  description="The terms for using Taxonomap, and credits for the data, photos and maps it shows."
  updated="3 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    Taxonomap is a free, non-commercial way to explore where species have been recorded. By using it you agree to these
    terms. They are short because the site is simple: there are no accounts and nothing to buy.
  </p>

  <h2>The data</h2>
  <p>
    Occurrence records, species names and map density come from{' '}
    <a href="https://www.gbif.org" rel="noopener">
      GBIF.org
    </a>
    , the Global Biodiversity Information Facility, and the thousands of institutions, projects and people who publish
    data through it. Each record is shared by its publisher under{' '}
    <a href={LICENCE_URLS.CC0} rel="license noopener">
      CC0
    </a>
    ,{' '}
    <a href={LICENCE_URLS['CC-BY']} rel="license noopener">
      CC BY
    </a>{' '}
    or{' '}
    <a href={LICENCE_URLS['CC-BY-NC']} rel="license noopener">
      CC BY-NC
    </a>
    , and Taxonomap credits its dataset wherever it shows one.
  </p>
  <p>
    Taxonomap shows the data as it comes from GBIF, live and unchanged apart from summaries such as counts and charts.
    Records can be wrong, incomplete, out of date or deliberately blurred (GBIF publishers often generalise the
    locations of sensitive species).{' '}
    <strong>Don’t rely on Taxonomap for safety, legal, conservation or other important decisions</strong>; check the
    original record and its publisher.
  </p>

  <h3>Reusing the data</h3>
  <p>
    If you use GBIF data in research, a report or a publication, download it from GBIF.org and cite the download’s DOI,
    as the{' '}
    <a href="https://www.gbif.org/terms" rel="noopener">
      GBIF data user agreement
    </a>{' '}
    asks. Charts and counts on Taxonomap are for exploring, not citing.
  </p>

  <h2>Photos</h2>
  <p>
    Photos come from records on GBIF and from{' '}
    <a href="https://www.inaturalist.org" rel="noopener">
      iNaturalist
    </a>
    . Taxonomap only shows photos under a Creative Commons licence or in the public domain, and shows each one’s licence
    and creator with it. Copyright stays with the photographer. If you reuse a photo, follow its licence: several only
    allow non-commercial use, and some don’t allow changes.
  </p>
  <p>
    Sounds on records and species pages follow the same rule: Taxonomap only plays those under a Creative Commons
    licence or in the public domain, shows each one’s licence and creator, and plays it from its publisher’s own site.
  </p>

  <h2>Species descriptions</h2>
  <p>
    The introduction under a species’ photos is the opening section of its English{' '}
    <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org" rel="noopener">
      Wikipedia
    </a>{' '}
    article, matched to the species through{' '}
    <a href="https://www.wikidata.org" rel="noopener">
      Wikidata
    </a>
    . It is available under{' '}
    <a href={LICENCE_URLS['CC-BY-SA']} rel="license noopener">
      CC BY-SA 4.0
    </a>
    , and each one links to its article.
  </p>

  <h2>Maps</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Plain basemap:{' '}
      <a href="https://openfreemap.org" rel="noopener">
        OpenFreeMap
      </a>
      , using{' '}
      <a href="https://openmaptiles.org" rel="noopener">
        OpenMapTiles
      </a>{' '}
      and map data ©{' '}
      <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright" rel="noopener">
        OpenStreetMap
      </a>{' '}
      contributors, available under the Open Database Licence.
    </li>
    <li>
      Satellite basemap:{' '}
      <a href="https://s2maps.eu" rel="noopener">
        Sentinel-2 cloudless
      </a>{' '}
      by EOX IT Services GmbH (contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data 2023), under{' '}
      <a href={LICENCE_URLS['CC-BY-NC-SA']} rel="license noopener">
        CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
      </a>
      .
    </li>
    <li>
      Place search:{' '}
      <a href="https://photon.komoot.io" rel="noopener">
        Photon
      </a>{' '}
      by komoot, with data © OpenStreetMap contributors.
    </li>
    <li>
      Map display:{' '}
      <a href="https://maplibre.org" rel="noopener">
        MapLibre GL JS
      </a>
      .
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Fair use of the site</h2>
  <p>
    Taxonomap sends your requests straight to GBIF and the other services above, so please use it as a person would.
    Don’t scrape it or automate heavy use; to work with data in bulk, use the{' '}
    <a href="https://techdocs.gbif.org/en/openapi/" rel="noopener">
      GBIF API
    </a>{' '}
    or downloads directly, under GBIF’s terms.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    Taxonomap is provided free and as it is. It may change, break or stop at any time, and we make no promise that it or
    the data it shows is accurate, complete or available. As far as the law allows, we aren’t liable for any loss from
    using it. Nothing here limits liability that can’t legally be limited.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    To report a problem, ask about these terms or flag content that shouldn’t be here, email{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>. Problems with a record or photo itself are best raised with its
    publisher, linked from the record. How we handle data is covered in the <a href="/privacy/">privacy notice</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
